These files make up the information that is transmitted to NCBI from SGD
for the creation of the Saccharomyces cerevisiae reference genome
sequence.  Each of the 17 chromosomes, 16 nuclear and one
mitochondrial, are defined within two files.  The fsa file is a FASTA
format sequence.  This is the known chromosomal sequence in one entry.
The second set of files, *.tbl, are in a tabular format that the NCBI Sequin
software will read. There are also corresonding GenBank format files
for each chromosome; these end in .gb

These tables are produced automatically by SGD from its database.  The
.gb, .sqn, and .tbl files are updated twice a year, and the .fsa files
are updated whenever a change to the chromosomal sequence occurs.

The archive directory contains past versions of the files described above.

------ 
NOTES: 
------ 
These files do not include sequences for merged or deleted ORFs, ORFs that 
SGD has classified as "Dubious", the 2-micron plasmid, or ORFs encoded on 
the 2-micron plasmid.

Sequence for the 2-micron plasmid can be obtained from GenBank at
http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/entrez/viewer.fcgi?db=nucleotide&val=nc_001398.

The start coordinate of the 2-micron plasmid sequence in SGD, in both
the database and on the Downloads site, has been shifted 1 kb upstream
relative to that provided in the GenBank record cited above.  As a
result, the 2-micron plasmid sequence in SGD starts upstream of FLP1
rather than in the middle of the FLP1 coding region.
